# What this plugin will not do

The page after somebody folded the format limit into a neighbouring entry and
left no heading behind. It still says in prose that it writes one subtitle
format, which is the half that makes this fixture worth having: a reader that
searched the page for those words rather than for the heading would report the
entry as present and compare the wrong sentence.

## It does not touch a subtitle that is already there

Held today. Recorded in #28. It writes one subtitle format and it leaves a file
already sitting at the target path alone, whatever that file is, and a `.srt`
somebody wrote by hand is the case that matters. The extension is here so a
reader looking anywhere on the page rather than inside one entry finds one.

## When this list is checked against the code

The closing section, which is about the list rather than a limit in it.
